These inherited config files changed. Re-read and apply their exact contents at every future intake. They are defaults/rules and do not remove your judgment to choose differently when warranted.

config/crew-dispatch.json
-----BEGIN config/crew-dispatch.json-----
{
  "rules": [
    {
      "when": "The task requires genuinely difficult, high-ambiguity, architectural, or multi-component implementation.",
      "use": {
        "harness": "pi",
        "model": "MiniMax-M3",
        "effort": "medium"
      },
      "why": "Reserve MiniMax-M3 for difficult implementation; the primary Firstmate/Codex performs review."
    },
    {
      "when": "The task requires live news, current events, X/Twitter data, market sentiment, or web-connected research.",
      "use": {
        "harness": "grok",
        "model": "grok-4.5",
        "effort": "high"
      },
      "why": "Grok Build is bundled with X subscription and provides live web search and X API access without token charges."
    },
    {
      "when": "The task is simple, low-risk, low-ambiguity bounded work, including browser automation/evidence capture under a precise procedure, and fresh applicable MiniMax effective remaining quota is above 50%. Captain directs Highspeed for new M2.7 work in this range; substantive diagnosis/complex fixes use the separately authorized MCode M3.1 Preview path, not this rule.",
      "use": {
        "harness": "pi",
        "model": "minimax/MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed",
        "effort": "medium"
      },
      "why": "Captain-approved temporary Highspeed routing. Recheck quota at every intake; at 50% or below use regular M2.7. Current general-scope quota is not proven model-specific accounting. Preserve running assignments; no permission changes or runtime fallback. Speed is distinct from reasoning effort."
    },
    {
      "when": "The task is routine day-to-day coding, bug fixing, test writing, refactoring, or feature implementation and the preceding Captain Highspeed rule does not apply.",
      "use": {
        "harness": "pi",
        "model": "MiniMax-M2.7",
        "effort": "medium"
      },
      "why": "Regular MiniMax-M2.7 remains the safe routine/default profile, including when applicable quota is 50% or below. Captain directs Highspeed above that threshold for bounded work through the preceding rule. Explicit current M3.1 MCode substantive-work instructions supersede the legacy M3 routing; never select retired M3 or silently substitute native M2.7 for substantive MCode work."
    }
  ],
  "default": [
    {
      "harness": "pi",
      "model": "MiniMax-M2.7",
      "effort": "medium"
    }
  ]
}
-----END config/crew-dispatch.json-----
